From 55d154e0f0119bc037455fb8fbef021085f7459f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: r3bb1t <49586603+r3bb1t@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 15:25:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] add 'cpuid_freq' option to control reporting of CPUID leaves
 0x15/0x16

CPU models since Skylake-X copy CPUID leaves 0x15 and 0x16 from real
hardware dumps, declaring a multi-GHz TSC while the emulated TSC advances
at the bochsrc 'ips' rate. Linux >= 4.8 trusts these leaves, never
calibrates against the PIT, and all TSC-derived guest time runs
declared_freq/ips (~875x at the default ips) slow. See issue #791.

The new 'cpu: cpuid_freq=' option keeps the hardware dump values by
default ('hardware', no behavior change), reports the leaves as not
enumerated ('none', the SDM-sanctioned encoding, restoring guest
timer-based calibration of the true rate), or derives them from the
emulated tick rate ('ips', for guests that trust CPUID).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
